From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: samtheruby <peasea1012@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 05:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cobalt): load TizenTube's script only into the YouTube
 page

TizenTube's script was added to every HTML document as it finished
loading. Cobalt's splash screen is a page of its own, so each start
downloaded and ran a second copy there (about 690 KB), which failed at
once without TizenTube's settings: "Config read failed" and "Uncaught
TypeError: Cannot convert undefined or null to object". Frames inside
a page would get a copy each too.

The script and the jsDelivr reachability check now go only into the
main frame of https://www.youtube.com, the page TizenTube is written for.
---
  third_party/blink/renderer/core/dom/document.cc | 9 +++++++--
  1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/dom/document.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/dom/document.cc
index 285aba907e8..e7df084390c 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/dom/document.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/dom/document.cc
@@ -4010,8 +4010,13 @@ void Document::ImplicitClose() {
 
   load_event_progress_ = kLoadEventInProgress;
 
-  // TizenTube userscript injection.
-  if (IsA<HTMLDocument>(this)) {
+  // TizenTube userscript injection, into the YouTube page only. Every HTML
+  // document closes here: Cobalt's splash screen (h5vcc-embedded://splash.html,
+  // a page of its own) and frames inside a page would each run another copy,
+  // which fails there without TizenTube's settings.
+  const KURL& page_url = Url();
+  if (IsA<HTMLDocument>(this) && GetFrame() && GetFrame()->IsMainFrame() &&
+      page_url.ProtocolIs("https") && page_url.Host() == "www.youtube.com") {
     Element* script_container = head();
 
     if (!script_container) {
-- 
2.47.3
